\ Validate selected structural lists before publishing a date.
\ Selection algorithms are not a substitute for checking invariants.
\ Every cutlet has a positive number of whole gate intervals;
\ the sum must equal the selected year's gate-span count.
\ Every month has between four and 123 days, inclusive; the
\ total must equal the selected year's duration in days.
\ Canonical names are distinct by construction, but an independent
\ audit verifies their ranges and the exact number assigned.
\ The audits only read committed lists and never recalculate a sauce.
\ They are safe to run repeatedly without changing the calendar.

A structure audit has
  a number called passed,
  a number called items checked,
  a number called units checked.

The structure audit is a structure audit.
The inspected cutlet piece is a cutlet piece.
The inspected cutlet name is a cutlet name assignment.
The inspected month length is a month length record.
The inspected month name is a month name assignment.
The scanned cutlet name is a cutlet name assignment.
The scanned month name is a month name assignment.
The audited label frequency is a number.

\ Name uniqueness is checked separately from the count of list nodes.
\ These small bounded linked lists have at most 17 or 47 entries, so a
\ second traversal is inexpensive and avoids machine-sized bit masks.
To count uses of a cutlet name given a number:
  Put 0 into the audited label frequency.
  Put the chosen cutlet names' first into the scanned cutlet name.
  Loop.
    If the scanned cutlet name is nil, break.
    If the scanned cutlet name's name index is the number,
      add 1 to the audited label frequency.
    Put the scanned cutlet name's next into the scanned cutlet name.
  Repeat.

To count uses of a month name given a number:
  Put 0 into the audited label frequency.
  Put the chosen month names' first into the scanned month name.
  Loop.
    If the scanned month name is nil, break.
    If the scanned month name's name index is the number,
      add 1 to the audited label frequency.
    Put the scanned month name's next into the scanned month name.
  Repeat.

To verify the selected cutlet partition:
  Put 1 into the structure audit's passed.
  Put 0 into the structure audit's items checked.
  Put 0 into the structure audit's units checked.
  Put the chosen cutlet pieces' first into the inspected cutlet piece.
  Loop.
    If the inspected cutlet piece is nil, break.
    If the inspected cutlet piece's span length is less than 1,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    Add 1 to the structure audit's items checked.
    Add the inspected cutlet piece's span length to the structure audit's units checked.
    Put the inspected cutlet piece's next into the inspected cutlet piece.
  Repeat.
  If the structure audit's items checked is not the selected cutlet count,
    put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
  If the structure audit's units checked is not the chosen year's span count,
    put 0 into the structure audit's passed.

To verify the selected cutlet names:
  Put 1 into the structure audit's passed.
  Put 0 into the structure audit's items checked.
  Put the chosen cutlet names' first into the inspected cutlet name.
  Loop.
    If the inspected cutlet name is nil, break.
    If the inspected cutlet name's name index is less than 1,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    If the inspected cutlet name's name index is greater than 17,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    Count uses of a cutlet name given the inspected cutlet name's name index.
    If the audited label frequency is not 1,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    Add 1 to the structure audit's items checked.
    Put the inspected cutlet name's next into the inspected cutlet name.
  Repeat.
  If the structure audit's items checked is not the selected cutlet count,
    put 0 into the structure audit's passed.

To verify the selected month lengths:
  Put 1 into the structure audit's passed.
  Put 0 into the structure audit's items checked.
  Put 0 into the structure audit's units checked.
  Put the chosen month lengths' first into the inspected month length.
  Loop.
    If the inspected month length is nil, break.
    If the inspected month length's month length days is less than 4,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    If the inspected month length's month length days is greater than 123,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    Add 1 to the structure audit's items checked.
    Add the inspected month length's month length days to the structure audit's units checked.
    Put the inspected month length's next into the inspected month length.
  Repeat.
  If the structure audit's items checked is not the selected month count,
    put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
  If the structure audit's units checked is not the chosen year's year length,
    put 0 into the structure audit's passed.

To verify the selected month names:
  Put 1 into the structure audit's passed.
  Put 0 into the structure audit's items checked.
  Put the chosen month names' first into the inspected month name.
  Loop.
    If the inspected month name is nil, break.
    If the inspected month name's name index is less than 1,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    If the inspected month name's name index is greater than 47,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    Count uses of a month name given the inspected month name's name index.
    If the audited label frequency is not 1,
      put 0 into the structure audit's passed; exit.
    Add 1 to the structure audit's items checked.
    Put the inspected month name's next into the inspected month name.
  Repeat.
  If the structure audit's items checked is not the selected month count,
    put 0 into the structure audit's passed.
